      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there are multiple NetworkRequests in the NetworkRequestInfo, then we will put all of them into mNetworkRequests, but only one of them will be released.\n\nIn general it seems like this method is pretty late to be doing this bookkeeping here in handleRegisterNetworkRequests, because this method is called for lots of types of requests, even internal ones. It seems better to put this code in handleRegisterNetworkRequest and handlerRegisterNetworkRequestWithIntent, which is much closer to where this code was being called before, and where AIUI we are guaranteed to have exactly one NetworkRequests in the NetworkRequestInfo.",
