      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, good point. I was confused by the fact that this code adds a new function instead of refactoring the existing function :-\\\n\nYou\u0027re right that if we do this then an app with CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL but not CONNECTIVITY_USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS won\u0027t be able to bring up restricted networks.\n\nDo you think you could remove the code duplication and make enforceConnectivityRestrictedNetworksPermission call check checkConnectivityRestrictedNetworksPermission? They do the same thing now.\n\nSeparately, there\u0027s a TODO in enforceConnectivityRestrictedNetworksPermission to remove CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL.\n\n        //  TODO: Remove this fallback check after all apps have declared\n        //   CONNECTIVITY_USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS.\n        mContext.enforceCallingOrSelfPermission(\n                android.Manifest.permission.CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL,\n                \"ConnectivityService\");\n\nMaybe you could clean up this TODO, so that, say, if SdkLevel.isAtLeastT(), then we don\u0027t check for CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL at all?\n\nCommented on aosp/2015175.",
